1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,702
Business Case 06 begins when an application reaches an authorized
interview-scheduling milestone.

2
00:00:05,702 --> 00:00:11,404
A versioned interview session completes with an eligible panel and due
scorecards.

3
00:00:11,404 --> 00:00:13,780
The governed record is INT-DEMO-001.

4
00:00:13,780 --> 00:00:19,006
The accountable actors are Candidate, Coordinator, Interviewer, Hiring
Manager, Candidate Support.

5
00:00:19,006 --> 00:00:26,134
This demonstration uses synthetic browser-memory data and creates no
database, provider, message or external-system effect.

6
00:00:26,134 --> 00:00:30,563
The action-level data-flow diagram defines 4 processes before product
navigation.

7
00:00:30,563 --> 00:00:38,537
Every process identifies the actor, screen, action, input, output,
business object, event, governed store, rule, denial and recovery.

8
00:00:38,537 --> 00:00:42,967
The highlighted path keeps each business grain and version distinct.

9
00:00:42,967 --> 00:00:45,250
Process 1, Candidate: Submit constraints.

10
00:00:45,250 --> 00:00:50,273
The action share availability produces versioned availability in the
Scheduling store.

11
00:00:50,273 --> 00:00:53,469
Process 2, Coordinator: Build session and panel.

12
00:00:53,469 --> 00:00:59,862
The action overlay availability and capacity produces conflict-free
session draft in the Interview ledger.

13
00:00:59,862 --> 00:01:02,602
Process 3, Candidate: Confirm or reschedule.

14
00:01:02,602 --> 00:01:09,908
The action respond to exact invitation produces confirmed, reschedule or
cancellation request in the Scheduling store.

15
00:01:09,908 --> 00:01:13,105
Process 4, Interviewer: Declare conflict or complete.

16
00:01:13,105 --> 00:01:19,955
The action open minimum-necessary brief produces completed session and
due scorecard in the Evidence ledger.

17
00:01:19,955 --> 00:01:22,890
The actual product route is /hr/interviews/INT-DEMO-001.

18
00:01:22,890 --> 00:01:30,230
It presents visual interview scheduling and panel capacity in the
surrounding recruitment or onboarding workspace.

19
00:01:30,230 --> 00:01:42,462
The screen remains a wireframe, but its identifiers, current state,
navigation, data relationships and action boundaries match the business
contract used by the connected workbench.

20
00:01:42,462 --> 00:01:45,277
The seeded workbench follows record INT-DEMO-001.

21
00:01:45,277 --> 00:02:03,574
Its governed fields are Candidate availability, Tue–Thu 09:00–13:00 PT;
Panel pool, 8 eligible interviewers; Selected panel, 3 , workload
balanced; Accommodation, Private coordinator channel; Session, Sep 3 ,
10:30 PT , 60 min; Conflicts, 0 current , 1 simulated.

22
00:02:03,574 --> 00:02:12,488
Field classifications remain visible so the presenter can distinguish
public, internal, confidential and restricted projections for the active
persona.

23
00:02:12,488 --> 00:02:16,684
With Recruiter selected, we perform confirm session and panel.

24
00:02:16,684 --> 00:02:21,345
The guard requires timezone, availability, workload, conflicts and
accommodations reconcile.

25
00:02:21,345 --> 00:02:33,931
The state changes from Draft v2 to Confirmed v3, records
InterviewScheduled, writes to the Scheduling ledger, and creates the
handoff: Candidate and panel receive current invitation preview.

26
00:02:33,931 --> 00:02:38,235
We now exercise the controlled exception: Simulate interviewer conflict.

27
00:02:38,235 --> 00:02:43,974
The prepared failure is Primary interviewer becomes unavailable on day
of session.

28
00:02:43,974 --> 00:02:54,017
Unsupported downstream work stops, successful prior evidence remains
intact, and the state-change receipt assigns explicit recovery without
hiding the failed attempt.

29
00:02:54,017 --> 00:02:57,115
The owned recovery is Substitute eligible interviewer.

30
00:02:57,115 --> 00:03:01,542
It reuses the governed business context without duplicating completed
effects.

31
00:03:01,542 --> 00:03:07,297
The new receipt preserves previous state, current state, actor, event
and correlation key.

32
00:03:07,297 --> 00:03:16,593
The control center and handoff inbox then expose the same recovery
through time-to-schedule, reschedules and panel capacity and
minimum-context next-actor work.

33
00:03:16,593 --> 00:03:19,672
Business Case 06 is complete.

34
00:03:19,672 --> 00:03:37,530
We demonstrated the level-two process contract, the actual product
route, governed field projections, the primary state transition, a
controlled exception, targeted recovery, causal dashboard evidence and
the next-actor handoff.

35
00:03:37,530 --> 00:03:44,920
A versioned interview session completes with an eligible panel and due
scorecards.

36
00:03:44,920 --> 00:03:51,693
Production identity, persistence, integrations and external delivery
remain separate implementation gates.
